		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17217&amp;sid=c326dd8f3b5cb0a93a3b5b6a0f173fc3#17217"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Mar 16, 2004 8:56 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17217&amp;sid=c326dd8f3b5cb0a93a3b5b6a0f173fc3"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Enters the Kindred Spirits and removes his helm.  His sweat and blood soaked face shows the wear of many battles in the last few days. 
<br />

<br />
Heading to the bar for a drink to quench his thirst, he notices a lone note.
<br />
He reads the note as a sad grin comes to his face.  "Ah, be well old friend.  Though we only raised our axes together once in the depths of Kaesora many moons ago, I shall miss you."  
<br />

<br />
Laying several plat on the bar, he draws two mugs of the Kindred Spirits Best and heads to a table near the smouldering fire.  He takes one glass and sets it beside him at an empty chair.  Raising the other he says in a hushed tone so as not to wake anyone:
<br />

<br />
"Be well and safe good Dwarf, may your Axe be sharp, your wit sharper and your enemies feel the bite of both!"  He downs his glass and leaves the other where he set it.
<br />

<br />
Rising from his chair he heads to his room to clean up a bit, rest some of his wounds and prepare to head back out, his work is not done yet.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Ceowulf
<br />
Champion to the Concordat Angelis</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
