		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17218&amp;sid=c326dd8f3b5cb0a93a3b5b6a0f173fc3#17218"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Mar 16, 2004 4:20 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17218&amp;sid=c326dd8f3b5cb0a93a3b5b6a0f173fc3"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Arriik had spent a lot of time on the note, and had crafted it with his finest calligraphy, signed it in his own hand, and sealed it with both his family crest and the seal of the Concordat.
<br />

<br />
"Any who leave shall be welcomed back, should they so desire.
<br />
Any who are of pure heart may join,
<br />
And any who seek a home are welcome.
<br />

<br />
We are now, have ever been, and ever shall be a Brotherhood,
<br />
Bound by Fate, sealed by Love, joined by Valor.
<br />
Though many no longer wear our tag,
<br />
We carry them always in our hearts,
<br />
They shall forever be our Brethren and Sistren,
<br />
As we shall always be theirs.
<br />

<br />
May the Gods guide and protect all members of the Concordat, past, present, and future.
<br />

<br />
Arriik Nobleblade, Prelate"</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
