				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Perhaps it's just a whisper of things long past, but for a brief moment the war weary paladin catches the barest glimpse of a clean cut figure, dressed simply in a green tunic and leather breeches. Off of the edge of her wine glass glints the carefully etched design of an axe. She wears the smile of someone far too sad for her age. At the moment he recognizes his former Prelate he turns, mostly out of reflex and in suprise that she might have returned. He hears the light-hearted laughter of a young human girl, maybe a druid, maybe simply his mind playing tricks on him. He is distracted for the briefest of moments, and when he looks back to where the elf was sitting, last seat at the edge of the bar, next to a much higher stool that was once reserved for a revered halfling, or in a pinch a crusty old dwarf, he sees nothing but a tip jar resting on the counter. He sighs, rubs his eyes for good measure, and turns to leave the bar.
<br />

<br />
-ooc- Don't think I've forgotten about you all. <img src="images/smiles/icon_wink.gif" alt="icon_wink.gif" border="0" /> Good luck, Sarxas, whatever path you choose. Hope you don't mind my poetic lisence. <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="icon_smile.gif" border="0" /></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
